    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-1-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-f2fe7294-8c86-47dc-8355-2a02f73cc20e": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 1",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant 1 - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Administrative Assistant 1 501431 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support CWA Full-Time Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Administrative Assistant 1 Department Org: Academic Personnel Admin - 106750 Employee Classification: H3 - Comm Workers of America FT Bargaining Unit: Communication Workers America Primary Location: MC AC Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:15 AM End Time: 5:00 PM Starting Rate: $19.17/hr. Job Description: Provides administrative support in various functional areas to support management and facilitate the daily work. Assist in program or departmental direction by relieving supervision of routine administrative duties. Provides information, prepares correspondence and reports, maintain calendars, monitor budget expenditures for the department, and resolves administrative problems. Minimum Qualifications: Education/Experience/Licensure: • Associates Degree in business management, secretarial sciences or related field required. • Must have Six (6) months administrative and/or secretarial experience performing similar duties for an upper-level management position required or a combination of experience and education will be accepted in lieu of higher education. • Expected to manage confidential information and maintain confidentiality at all times, including FERPA. THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO Job Description / Class Specification Administrative Assistant 1 Page 2 • Must be flexible, able to multi-task and manage multiple high priority demands, and rearrange priorities as needed. Demonstrated skill in time management is required. • Knowledge of organizational and general office procedures and operations and the ability to analyze and make recommendations. • Knowledge of the methods, principles and techniques associated with research, data collection and report writing. • Knowledge of generally accepted accounting practices and procedures and the procedures and practices of preparing and controlling operating and capital budgets. • Knowledge of contract development, administration, and monitoring, as required. • Knowledge and ability in the use of computers and peripheral equipment such as printers. • Ability to analyze and interpret data and write reports. • Ability to deal tactfully and equitably with people and to effectively communicate. • Ability to use personal computers and applications necessary to collect and analyze data and access and produce budget and procurement documents and changes. • Ability to effectively communicate and carry out written and/or verbal instruction; detail oriented and accurate. • Ability to attend meetings. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) d8afab3e Last Name (required) 6bfe9101 Email (required) 0c312a51 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Cardiac Sonographer 2 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Heart Station - 109070 Cardiac Sonographer 2, Full Time (8:00am - 17:30pm) 5 8's Saturday rotation\nNo Sundays, Call is on rotation, Holiday call is on rotation.\nMay Underfill with Cardiac Sonographer 1. Ekg Technician I Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Heart Station - 109070 EKG Technician I, Part Time, Sunday - Saturday (6:30am - 11:00pm).\nRotate, Weekends/Holidays. Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio. Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio. Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio Dept. of Cell and Cancer Biology - 107500 Cell & Cancer Biology Faculty Position Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 63aebc76 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Administrative Support CWA Full-Time Administration Administrative Support CWA Full-Time Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) f956c4c8 Last Name (required) fd11eab2 Email (required) 06379aeb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination