n: May 7 2026 Reporting to the Director, this position will assist in the daily operation and functioning of the office which resides in the Center for Advocacy and Student Experience (CASE) . This position will be responsible for assisting in the resolution of complaints of alleged violations of the Student Code of Conduct, serving as an Administrative Hearing Officer, investigating student and student group/organization misconduct, and providing advocacy for students experiencing varying levels of crisis.\nThis position will also be responsible for developing and executing office outreach and programming, collaborating with other areas across campus, assisting with the training of University Hearing Officers and Hearing Boards, and working with the Director to develop and advance a Conflict Resolution Program. This position will also be responsible for preparing materials for hearings, generating reports/data using the conduct database, and serving on University and Divisional committees. Read more Legal Assistant, HSC Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH Office Of Legal Affairs - 104890 Full-Time Legal None Staff - Full-Time Opening on: Apr 30 2026 This role directly supports the Sr. Associate General Counsel, Sr. Associate General Counsel- Healthcare, the Contract Compliance Officer, and the Legal Nurse Specialist performing a variety of duties such as preparing legal documents and correspondence, docketing cases, managing all legal files and providing information and direction to others. This position allows access to and deals with highly confidential information related to litigation, legal issues, strategies, and positions related to the University and its subsidiaries, including labor unions of The University of Toledo. Read more Phys Ther Asst Lic I Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH OP-Physical Therapy - 109320 AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Staff - Full-Time Opening on: Jan 27 2026 Full-Time, 1st Shift\nOPERS/ Medical/ Dental/ Vision\n\