    "https://www.utoledo.edu/jobs/": {
      "title": "UToledo Careers",
      "description": "UToledo Careers Applicant Login Benefits Applicant Login Benefits Menu Menu Admission + Admission Undergraduate Online Transfer International Graduate/Professional College Credit Plus Guest Admitted/New Rocket Academics + Explore Majors and Programs Search Syllabus Library Academic Colleges Arts, Social Sciences and Education Business and Innovation Engineering Graduate Studies Health and Human Services Honors Law Medicine and Life Sciences Natural Sciences and Mathematics Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences University College Research + Research News Research and Sponsored Programs Grant Development Technology Transfer Research Compliance Human Research Protection Program Economic Development About + About UToledo Mission Administration Accreditation Student Outcomes Expression on Campus Invited Speakers Athletics Alumni UToledo Health Giving MyUT Main Menu UToledo Careers Menu About Visit Contact Us Main Campus Center for Administrative Support Hours: 8:30 a.m. to 5 p.m. Phone: 419.530.4747 Fax: 419.530.1490 HumanResourcesDepartment@utoledo.edu UToledo Careers Watch ceremonies Watch ceremonies Watch ceremonies OPENING DOORS. TRANSFORMING TOMORROWS. The University of Toledo is dedicated to improving the world through discovery, helping\n                        students succeed and patients heal. If you can advance our mission by pursuing your\n                        lifeâs purpose with a passion, weâd love to have you join our team! WHY WORK AT UToledo? As a major public research university, UToledo offers a large network of richly diverse\n                        people and services, generous benefits and a healthy work-life balance, all on vibrant\n                        campuses featuring lots of green space. And, because the University is the second-largest\n                        employer in northwest Ohio, our faculty and staff have many options for professional\n                        growth and personal job satisfaction. Search our jobs. Fuel your future. UTMC positions requiring current AHA CPR certification ( Policy 3364-100-50-33 ) must be completed within the orientation period. All Open Positions Current Employees UToledo Bargaining Unit Bidding Clery Act | EEO | Accessibility | Immigration Notices | Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws © 2020 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us Last Updated: 8/20/26"
