    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/seasonal-employee-hourly-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-87fe5cd6-dcec-4971-aadb-c29847c870d3": {
      "title": "Seasonal Employee Hourly",
      "description": "Seasonal Employee Hourly - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Seasonal Employee Hourly 501380 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH None Part-Time Research Seasonal Show More Show Less Staff - Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Title: Seasonal Employee Hourly Department Org: Molecular, Cellular & Dev Biology - 101220 Employee Classification: H6 - Intermittent - Seasonal Hourly Bargaining Unit: Bargaining Unit Exempt Primary Location: MC AC Shift: 1 Posted Salary: $30.00 per hour Job Description: *Isolating and identifying strawberry endophytic fungi *Characterization of the beneficial endophytic fungi against plant biotic and abiotic stresses Minimum Qualifications: Degree from plant protection or plant pathology program. Experience working on beneficial fungi, such as Trichoderma or Clonostachys fungi. Preferred Qualifications: Degree from plant protection or plant pathology program. Experience working on beneficial fungi, such as Trichoderma or Clonostachys fungi. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 51de50e5 Last Name (required) a0ac8035 Email (required) a8d4ef2f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment,