      "description": "Program Coordinator, Athletic Video Production - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Program Coordinator, Athletic Video Production 501512 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Athletics Full-Time Marketing/Communication None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Program Coordinator, Athletic Video Production Department Org: Athletic-Market & Promotn - 104950 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AC Shift: 1 Posted Salary: Minimum $ 45,000 Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: This role will assist Toledo Athletics in developing the department’s video elements to promote the University’s 16 varsity sports, events/games, Rocket Fund, ticket sales, and help with creating a positive and enhanced game day atmosphere and recruiting initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: •Bachelor’s degree required in Communications or a related field. •Must have 2-3 years of professional experience in sports, communications, or related field. •Must have working knowledge of the following Software: Xpression, Daktronics, and Motion Rocket Preferred Qualifications: •The ideal candidate must have a full understanding of video production software, video and broadcast quality, expert level experience in Adobe Creative Suite, Final Cut Pro and other non-linear video editing software, proper lighting techniques and composition, video sound, camera operation, emerging technologies and equipment as they develop while understanding the college athletics landscape. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for t