    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-to-the-chair-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-1723055f-7d04-4284-862f-185fdb2d5e67": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Chair",
      "description": "Assistant to the Chair - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant to the Chair 501540 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support Full-Time None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant to the Chair Department Org: Neurosciences - 107510 Employee Classification: J1 - Salaried Full Time HSC Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: HSC C Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:30 a.m. End Time: 5:00 p.m. Salary: Salary will be based on education and experience Job Description: Applicant works with minimal supervision from the department chair and the Department Administrator to plan, direct and manage daily department operations and activities. Applicant will complete duties and responsibilities as described below to provide high-quality, cost-effective management of department administrative and budgetary functions. Minimum Qualifications: Rank (List in order of importance) List of Job Duties (Start each duty with an action verb such as “operate,” “repair,” or “perform” etc.) 1 Assist chair in the management of research programs for all faculty within the department. Duties may include, but are not limited to: thorough knowledge of faculty research interests; identify funding opportunities; assist in grant development, preparation, submission, and annual reporting; oversee protocol preparations and renewals; and review publications for accuracy. Maintain liaison with representatives of other departments to establish and maintain appropriate interface. Establish and maintain appropriate network of professional contacts. Maintain currency with professional organizations and publications. Attend and participate in meetings, conferences, etc. Provide assistance on institutional committees as recording secretary as necessary. Represent the department at institutional meetings and activities and to external agencies and organizations as assigned. Design departmental printed materials, including presentation materials, as needed. Develops or maintains proficiency in NIH Assist. 2 Assists in management of education, seminars, greeting department visitors and assisting lost patients, attend to budgetary matters as needed. Duties may include but are not limited to: management of Blackboard and Exam Soft, proctoring exams and reviews; reconciling indexes, purchasing; accounts payable; and pcard reporting. 3 Assist chair and department administrator in management of day-to-day activities of the department chair including, but not limited to: calendar appointments, preparation of correspondence and email; travel arrangements; p-card reconciliation; preparation of general correspondence and email; and ad hoc duties as assigned (e.g., renovation projects, meeting minutes). 4 Assist with faculty recruitment as needed. Duties may include: travel arrangements, preparation of itineraries, expense reimbursement, and dinner reservations. 5 Organize departmental events (e.g. research forums, technology showcases) from inception to end. 6 Special projects and other administrative duties as assigned. TOTAL Preferred Qualifications: Qualifications/Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Education/experience/licensing: Bachelor Degree in business administration, management, public relations or other related field required OR 5 year’s office environment experience may be accepted in lieu of degree. Excellent computer skills required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). Knowledge of Publisher, Photoshop, Illustrator, Blackboard, and API helpful. Communication and other skills: Ability to organize, prioritize and efficiently coordinate various responsibilities and job duties. Ability to establish constructive interpersonal relationships. Ability to work independently, be self-motivated, and be proactive to avoid negative consequences. Ability to respond to rapidly changing business environment. Ability to multitask (e.g., preparing grants, budgets and luncheon meetings simultaneously). Ability to maintain high degree of confidentiality. Excellent written, verbal and culturally appropriate communication skills. Analysis, assessment and evaluation skills. Appreciation for scientific research and an understanding of basic science helpful. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Acc