    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/nurse-navigator-vascular-surgery-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-0dfdc170-3da3-4835-8bb1-acab00f00a7c": {
      "title": "Nurse Navigator- Vascular Surgery",
      "description": "Nurse Navigator- Vascular Surgery - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Nurse Navigator- Vascular Surgery 501529 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH Healthcare Positions None Nursing Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Nurse Navigator- Vascular Surgery Department Org: OP-Clinic-Admin - 110270 Employee Classification: J1 - Salaried Full Time HSC Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:00 am End Time: 4:30 pm Posted Salary: Starting at $68,077 - $93,000 Float: False Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: False Job Description: The Vascular Surgery Nurse Navigator serves as a clinician and clinical administrator for the Wound and Vascular surgery department. Navigates vascular and wound surgery, education patient, evaluation of documentation and proper charging related to the care delivered in the outpatient setting, and responds to patient, provider and referring physician inquiries. Promotes patient safety by adhering to institutional and departmental policies and by practicing high standards of care. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Current RN licensure in the State of Ohio. 2. BSN preferred 3. Recent clinical experience in specialty field preferred. 4. Proficiency in selected Microsoft Office 5. Exhibits accuracy, integrity and flexibility; is punctual and dependable. 6. Possesses organizational, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills. 7. Demonstrates ability to work with self-direction and effectiveness under minimal supervision. 8. Demonstrates excellent written and verbal communication skills; possesses group facilitation skills. 9. Current BLS required Preferred Qualifications: BSN preferred Recent clinical experience in specialty field preferred. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1d3ede8a Last Name (required) 60fbe418 Email (required) b92e164b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University