    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/job-coach-preets-instructor-toledo-transition-seasonal-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Job Coach & PreEts Instructor, Toledo Transition, Seasonal",
      "description": "Job Coach & PreEts Instructor, Toledo Transition, Seasonal - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Job Coach & PreEts Instructor, Toledo Transition, Seasonal 501528 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic None Part-Time Seasonal Student Affairs Student Services Show More Show Less Staff - Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Title: Job Coach & PreEts Instructor, Toledo Transition, Seasonal Department Org: Dept of Exercise & Rehab Sciences - 107720 Employee Classification: H6 - Intermittent - Seasonal Hourly Bargaining Unit: Bargaining Unit Exempt Primary Location: MC AC Job Description: The Toledo Transition (T2) Program is seeking to hire Job Coach & PreEts Instructors. This position provides instructional, operational, and collaborative leadership to support students with disabilities in developing skills for post-secondary education, employment, and independent living. Job Coach & PreEts Instructors deliver classroom instruction, facilitate campus and community experiences, and work closely with the Program Administrator to ensure high quality programming aligned with university and state guidelines. The role also includes teaching Pre Employment Transition Services (Pre ETS) content to support students’ vocational readiness. Key Responsibilities • Job Coach — Provides support to Toledo Transition students through OOD job search and job coaching. • Classroom Instruction — Teach course content related to executive functioning, independent living, self advocacy, social participation, and disability awareness on a contingent basis. • Pre ETS Instruction — Deliver Pre Employment Transition Services content, including workplace readiness, career exploration, self advocacy, and soft skills development; collaborate with state and community partners as needed. • Collaboration with Program Administrator — Work closely with the Program Administrator to align curriculum, ensure compliance, coordinate staffing, and support strategic planning for program growth. • Student Support — Provide individualized and group support, assist students in developing routines, time management strategies, and self regulation skills. • Stakeholder Communication — Serve as a liaison to families, campus partners, community organizations, and collaborating departments to ensure cohesive support for students. • Data & Documentation — Maintain accurate records, track student outcomes, and prepare reports for internal review, accreditation, and grant related activities. • Training & Mentorship — Support onboarding and development of instructors, graduate assistants, and student workers involved in T2 programming. • Safety & Compliance — Ensure adherence to university policies, disability services guidelines, and best practices in post-secondary education. Minimum Qualifications: • High School Diploma • Familiarity with OOD provider processes • Classroom Instruction • Computer literate Preferred Qualifications: • Associates Degree • Background in Special Education Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f430094c Last Name (required) 56e346b9 Email (required) 0465c46c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f73a2e0f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic None Part-Time Seasonal Student Affairs Student Services Academic None Part-Time Seasonal Student Affairs Student Services Employment Type Staff - Temporary Staff - Temporary Locations Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 95b628f7 Last Name (required) 4b9369f8 Email (required) 98f945b0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
