    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/events-coordinator-main-campus-student-affairs-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Events Coordinator - Main Campus - Student Affairs Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Events Coordinator 501484 Main Campus - Student Affairs Toledo, OH Administration CWA Full-Time Student Affairs Student Services Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Events Coordinator Department Org: Rocket Career Center - 103720 Employee Classification: H3 Bargaining Unit: CWA Primary Location: MC SA Shift: 1 Posted Salary: Starting at $18.71/hr. Job Description: General Summary The Event Coordinator is a vital member of the Rocket Career Center team, responsible for leading efforts in data management, event logistics, and Handshake platform administration. This position ensures smooth operations across a wide range of functions, including compiling and analyzing data for reports, managing departmental budgets, and maintaining accurate records for presentations and major project plans for events. Additionally, the role serves as the primary administrator for Handshake—reviewing and approving employers and job postings, managing events and career fairs within the platform, and providing technical support to students, staff, and external partners. The successful candidate will: • Support Office Administration: Serve as a primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners; coordinate schedules and requests; manage purchasing and budget tracking; maintain records; prepare reports; and support the Center’s communications and web content. • Coordinate Events and Programs: Plan and coordinate the logistics for career fairs, employer events, workshops, presentations, and other programs, including registration, communications, facilities and technology needs, purchasing, financial transactions, attendance tracking, and post-event reporting. • Administer Handshake: Serve as a primary administrator for the University’s Handshake career platform by reviewing and approving employers, jobs, events, and career fairs; troubleshooting user issues; supporting students, staff, and employers; and developing and maintaining reports through Handshake Analytics. This is a detail-oriented, data-driven position requiring a high degree of accuracy in managing information, budgets, records, and reports. The successful candidate will be comfortable working with data, analyzing information, identifying trends or discrepancies, and using technology and analytical tools to produce accurate reports that support decision-making. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and technical skills are essential for success in this role. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree required and minimum of one (1) year related work experience, or a combination of education and experience. • Knowledge of and experience with Microsoft Excel, Word, Outlook and PowerPoint and Adobe Acrobat required. Preferred Qualifications: • Higher education experience preferred. • Experience with webforms and Microsoft forms preferred • Experience with Handshake, online job platform, a plus. • Experience with Canva, graphic design platform, a plus • Experience with Modern Campus CMS or other website editing platforms, a plus Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
