    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/electronic-technologist-2-college-of-engineering-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Electronic Technologist 2, College of Engineering",
      "description": "Electronic Technologist 2, College of Engineering - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Electronic Technologist 2, College of Engineering 501455 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic CWA Full-Time Information Technology Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Electronic Technologist 2, College of Engineering Department Org: Dean-Engineering - 101850 Employee Classification: H3 - Comm Workers of America FT Bargaining Unit: Communication Workers America Primary Location: MC AC Shift: 1 Start Time: End Time: Posted Salary: Float: {bOther1} Rotate: {bOther2} On Call: {bOther3} Travel: {bOther4} Weekend/Holiday: {bOther5} Job Description: The Electronic Technologist II supports electronic instrumentation needs for the College of Engineering instructional laboratories, including training and supervision of students using the electronic equipment. Specific duties include: 1. Setting up, maintaining, and repairing electronic and computer instrumentation used in various instructional laboratories. 2. Supervising, coordinating, and assisting with research, capstone design, and course-related activities in assigned laboratories. 3. Providing support for courses in other assigned instructional laboratory spaces. 4. Scheduling, performing, and/or approving all work-related to setup, maintenance, relocation, and operation of equipment in assigned instructional laboratory spaces. 5. Providing training to teaching assistants and students in laboratory safety and overseeing their activities to ensure safe operation of laboratory equipment. 6. Working with faculty and staff to order, track receipt, and deliver supplies, equipment, materials, and other items for assigned instructional laboratories. 7. Providing support for recruiting events for prospective students, such as daily tours or workshops. Minimum Qualifications: Education/experience/licensing: • A bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, electronics engineering. or equivalent; or. at least five years of experience working in a related industry. • Ability to design, setup, and repair electronic instrumentation and computer equipment. • Ability to read and implement circuit schematics. • Ability to design, program. and operate computer-controlled laboratory instrumentation. Communication and other skills: • Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with undergraduate and graduate students, faculty, and other staff on instructional and research projects. • Demonstrated ability to present ideas and communicate with non-technical visitors to the laboratories. • Ability to work with university and outside professionals on engineering design and construction projects. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) c3450665 Last Name (required) eba1b45a Email (required) 970753a1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
