    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/administrative-director-transplant-service-line-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Administrative Director, Transplant Service Line",
      "description": "Administrative Director, Transplant Service Line - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Administrative Director, Transplant Service Line 501501 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH Administration Full-Time Hospital Administration None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Administrative Director, Transplant Service Line Department Org: Employee Classification: J1 - Salaried Full Time HSC Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:30am End Time: 5:00pm Posted Salary: Job Description: The Administrative Director for Transplant Service Line provides strategic and operational leadership for the UTMC Center for Transplant Medicine and affiliated clinics and outreach services across UToledo Health. This role delivers oversight and coordination of operations within the transplant service line ensuring alignment with UTH’s mission of academic excellence, patient-centered care, and continuous improvement. Minimum Qualifications: • Master’s degree or higher degree in healthcare, business, education or related field required; MBA or MHA preferred. • Seven plus years of previous management experience required with at least five in years in a relevant healthcare setting with transplant services experience preferred. • Fellow of the American College of Healthcare Executives certification preferred. • Experience, training, and/or certification in operations improvement methodologies (i.e. lean six sigma) desired. • Tactful, respectful, and courteous in dealing with patients, visitors, students, residents, physicians, and staff. • Able to maintain effective working relationships with personnel and medical staff. • Successfully completed orientation program within 90 days. • Demonstrates ability to work with self-direction with minimal supervision. • Demonstrates excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work closely with multiple teams. • Previous experience with accreditation standards including the Joint Commission. • Proficiency in Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, or similar software applications with proven knowledge of standard computer manipulation required. • Excellent communication and interpersonal skills in both oral and written format. • Ability to successfully operate and manage others in complex, high paced team-based environments requiring sophisticated interpersonal communication and conflict resolution skills. • Ability to develop and maintain professional, service-oriented working relationships with patients, families, physicians, nurses, co-workers, supervisors and others. • Ability to analyze data, perform multiple tasks and work independently. • Must be able to understand and comply with policies and procedures. • Possess excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. • Ability to work collaboratively in a professional office environment with a high-performance team of professionals in partnership toward common objectives. Preferred Qualifications: • MBA or MHA preferred. • At least five in years in a relevant management experience in a healthcare setting with transplant services experience preferred. • Fellow of the American College of Healthcare Executives certification preferred Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cdb4b501 Last Name (required) f0fedde8 Email (required) 9ac6e34a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of 