    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/cardiac-sonographer-2-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-6568b42b-dc09-4d93-bc6d-3cc66f6875d5": {
      "title": "Cardiac Sonographer 2",
      "description": "Cardiac Sonographer 2 - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Cardiac Sonographer 2 501458 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Cardiac Sonographer 2 Department Org: Heart Station - 109070 Employee Classification: B5 - Unclass Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:00am End Time: 17:30pm Posted Salary: $45.14 - $52.82 Float: False Rotate: True On Call: True Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: As a member of the health care team, performs non-invasive cardiac diagnostic testing including M-mode echocardiograms, 2-Dimensional and 3-Dimensional Sector scans, Cardiac Doppler, Colorflow Imaging, and measurement of Ejection Fraction by echocardiogram on patients who are adolescent, and adults at UTMC. Assists the physician in the performance of Transesophageal Echocardiograms. Performs Stress Exercise Echocardiograms in the Heart Station with the Stress Laboratory personnel. Maintains digital computer system. All employees must adhere to the following at all times: • Employee is expected to adhere to UTMC Service Values including iCare standards at all times. • Adheres to hospital policies and procedures as well as addresses patient safety, performance improvement, and quality of care issues. 1. Adheres to NPSG 09.02.01 by following the Morse Fall Scale to assess all patients for their risk of falling. 2. Adheres to NPSG 07.01.01 by effectively washing hands when going from one patient to the next. • Knowledgeable about patient safety and quality of care issues. Able to recognize safety issues in the department and handles incidents per institutional and/or departmental policies and procedures. If safety issues were identified; all issues were handled timely and appropriately. • Department education and training focus has a direct impact on patient safety and reduces unsafe working conditions for employees. • Employee attends and follows all department specific safety education and training in an effort to create a safe work environment. 1. Recognizes Frayed Cord: Reports equipment dysfunction in timely manner. Make sure alternate process is in place and action is taken. Reduces adverse results or impact to patient care and the employee. 2. Recognize exposure to Blood: Worked as a team to limit exposure and create a safe work environment. Safety concerns: The manager has been timely with staff training and education. Wiping up spills. 3. Follows standardized approach for handoff communication Follows policy for communication including the opportunity to ask and respond to questions Minimum Qualifications: Qualifications/Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Required Education/Experience/Licensing: • Associate degree in Cardiovascular Technology or higher relevant degree required or ten (10) years of experience in performing Echocardiograms. • Must be registered for five (5) years and have performed Echocardiograms for five (5) years after being registered. The work experience must be recent, relevant and proficiency in independent performance of exams documented. Experience in school will not be counted. • Computer knowledge required. • AHA/CPR certification required in Basic Life Support Health Care Provider course identified by the Heart Station/Cardiology Clinic policy. • Experience in non-invasive cardiology preferred. Communication and other skills: • Must be able to be on-call and work independently when called in. • Must be able to be on-call and be in to the hospital within 1 hour when called in. MAY UNDERFILL WITH CARDIAC SONOGRAPHER 1 • Associate degree in Cardiovascular Technology or higher relevant degree required • Must be registered in Adult Echocardiography through ARDMS or obtain within six (6) months of hire. • Computer knowledge required. • AHA/CPR certification required in Basic Life Support Health Care Provider • Experience in non-invasive cardiology preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
