    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/server-administrator-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Server Administrator",
      "description": "Server Administrator - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Server Administrator 501545 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Full-Time Information Technology None Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Server Administrator Department Org: IT Personnel - 105780 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:00 a.m. End Time: 5:00 p.m. Posted Salary: Float: False Rotate: True On Call: True Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: False Job Description: This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. This position participates in medium-to-large server projects under the direction of senior server administration personnel and the Manager Server Administration. The position performs follow-up activities to ensure high levels of customer satisfaction are maintained. All members of the University Server Team rotate on-call responsibilities to ensure 24x7x365 availability of the enterprise academic, administrative, and clinical systems. Minimum Qualifications: o Bachelor’s Degree in a relevant area of study (i.e., Computer Science, Electronics, Information Systems, etc.) is required. Other areas of study will be considered with five years of relevant experience. o Three years of increasing experience in the areas of server administration, systems management, hypervisor administration, and network management in a medium to large organization. o Experience in troubleshooting server hardware and software problems. o Advanced knowledge of the Windows Server operating systems, or Red Hat Enterprise Linux/Oracle Enterprise Linux systems. Communication and other skills o Punctuality, regular attendance, and dependability. o Customer service skills, controlled demeanor, and stress tolerance. o Organization, follow-through, and attention to detail. o Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. o Ability to work well in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications: o Experience working in either a healthcare or academic environment. o Microsoft Server certification (2016+ MCSE, MCSA), or Red Hat Certified System Administrator (RHCSA) / Oracle Certified Professional. o Detailed knowledge of PowerShell scripting or programming. o Epic EMR ECSA Web and Service Servers and/or Epic ODB experience with current Epic certification(s). Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 3b5e6bba Last Name (required) ba4d8f2b Email (required) 3502dea3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. Mental Health Aide Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Senior Behavioral Health - 110100 Mental Health Aide assists the Staff Nurse and Therapists, in providing delegated tasks on the nursing unit. Assists in maintaining a clean and orderly work area. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9212cd23 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Full-Time Information Technology None Full-Time Information Technology None Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) d9c973e2 Last Name (required) 2a991c0f Email (required) 380f7d16 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
