    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/creative-director-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Creative Director",
      "description": "Creative Director - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Creative Director 501516 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Full-Time Marketing/Communication None Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Creative Director Department Org: University Marketing - 104840 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: On-Site at the University of Toledo - Main Campus Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:15 am End Time: 5:00 pm Posted Salary: $74,000 - $84,000 Job Description: As a member of the Marketing and Communications leadership team, the Creative Director shapes and advances the creative vision for The University of Toledo and UToledo Health across all marketing and communications channels. Working collaboratively with leaders across marketing, communications, digital, web, and health system partners, this position guides creative development from concept through execution, ensuring every touchpoint reflects the institution's brand, strategic priorities, and commitment to excellence. The Creative Director leads and mentors a multidisciplinary creative team, fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and continuous improvement. This leader oversees integrated creative initiatives across print, digital, web, social media, photography, video, and emerging platforms, delivering compelling work that advances institutional, academic, and healthcare goals while strengthening the reputation of both the University and UToledo Health. The Creative Director translates strategy into memorable brand experiences that differentiate the University and UToledo Health in an increasingly competitive higher education and healthcare landscape. As the institution's creative champion, this leader inspires bold ideas, strengthens and protects the brand, and balances creativity with measurable marketing outcomes. Impact on the Organization: • Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution. • Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities. • Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. Minimum Qualifications: Education/experience/licensing: • Bachelor's degree in graphic design, visual communications, fine arts, or a related field. • Minimum Seven years of progressively responsible experience in creative direction, brand leadership, or integrated marketing, including experience leading multidisciplinary creative teams. • Demonstrated success developing and executing integrated creative campaigns across print, digital, web, social media, video, and emerging platforms. • Experience building, mentoring, and leading high-performing creative teams while managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. • Higher education, healthcare, or other complex, mission-driven organizational experience preferred. • Strong, conceptual portfolio demonstrating big idea thinking across print, digital, social and integrated campaigns. • Experience working in a fast-paced, in-house agency environment. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 5c160bf4 Last Name (required) 60d9bdc3 Email (required) 6517fd86 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Mental Health Aide Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Senior Behavioral Health - 110100 Mental Health Aide assists the Staff Nurse and Therapists, in providing delegated tasks on the nursing unit. Assists in maintaining a clean and orderly work area. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 91527c93 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Full-Time Marketing/Communication None Full-Time Marketing/Communication None Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 53e4bbb3 Last Name (required) aaf8a3aa Email (required) 173f9da1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
