    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-american-political-thought-american-constitutionalism-american-history-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (American political thought; American constitutionalism; American history)",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (American political thought; American constitutionalism; American history) - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (American political thought; American constitutionalism; American history) 501480 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic Faculty - Regular Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (American political thought; American constitutionalism; American history) Department Org: Inst Am Cons Thought & Ldrship - 114470 Employee Classification: F3 - Faculty 9 Month Non AAUP Bargaining Unit: Other Non AAUP Primary Location: MC AD Job Description: The Institute of American Constitutional Thought & Leadership invites applications for multiple open rank faculty positions to start in fall 2027. The Institute is an interdisciplinary and public-spirited center at the University of Toledo dedicated to the foundational principles, institutions, and texts of America’s constitutional order and of greater Western Civilization. We are an honors-level “school within a school” at UToledo, providing courses, degree programs, and public events that enhance the humanities offerings at the University of Toledo and serve the broader northwest Ohio community. The Institute’s faculty are committed to building an academic community in which civic life and the life of the mind flourish. These scholars and teachers are dedicated to examining timeless questions while addressing timely problems in American civic life. As the heart of our academic community, they advance the Institute’s mission by making meaningful contributions to their academic disciplines, teaching and mentoring students, modeling collegiality, sustaining robust scholarly activity, and serving the university and the broader Ohio community. Faculty will teach up to five courses per academic year. The appointments and tenure for all the Institute’s faculty are held within the Institute. The Institute offers a minor in Constitutional Studies; a minor in Science, Technology, and Society (STS); and will soon launch a Constitutional Studies Major. Faculty in the Institute ordinarily teach multiple sections of CLT 2000: The American Constitutional Tradition as part of their regular teaching loads. This course serves as an entry to the Institute’s academic programs; it also satisfies a civic education requirement for every undergraduate in Ohio institutions of higher education. Ideal candidates will be prepared to teach multiple sections of this course, which introduces students to key readings in American political thought, American constitutionalism, early modern political philosophy, and great speeches by American statesmen. Candidates should be familiar with and embrace the Institute’s mission as defined by ORC Sec. 3364.07 (B), (C), which is to educate university students in (A) the core texts and great debates of Western civilization; (B) the principles, ideals, and institutions of the American and Ohio political order; and (C) the foundations of responsible leadership and informed citizenship. This is a full-time position. Salaries are highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants should explain how their scholarship and teaching experience reflect and support the Institute’s mission. The candidate should also indicate interest in interdisciplinary teaching, research, and collaboration. The Institute’s faculty must be self-motivated, well-organized, and committed to the extraordinary work of building up a new institution. The successful candidate will need to interact comfortably and confidently with a broad internal and external constituency, representing the University and the Institute with professionalism. Application Instructions: A complete application must include: 1. A current curriculum vitae 2. A letter of application that describes the candidates teaching philosophy, research plan, and understanding of the Institute’s mission 3. Evidence of teaching excellence 4. A sample of scholarly writing from within the last three years 5. Names and contact information for three references are required. Recommendations will be requested for selected candidates. The letter of application should describe the candidate’s interest in the Institute’s mission and the candidate’s understanding of civic education. The letter should also explain how the candidate is prepared to support that mission through teaching, research, and service (such as extracurricular programs, student recruitment, etc.). All application documents should be uploaded at utoledo.edu/jobs. Review of applications will begin immediately, and interviews will be conducted on a rolling basis until the positions are filled. The deadline for priority consideration is November 13, 2026. The position start date is August 2027. Please address any inquiries to Stefanie Bias at Stefanie.Bias@utoledo.edu. Letters of application should be addressed to: Jonathan Culp, Ph.D. Director, Institute of American Constitutional Thought and Leadership University of Toledo 2801 West Bancroft, MS 507 Toledo, Ohio 43606 E-mail: Jonathan.Culp@UToledo.edu Minimum Qualifications: Requirements: 1. A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree is required, conferred by August 1, 2027. 2. A commitment to and demonstrated understanding of the Institute’s mission. 3. A robust research agenda. 4. Evidence of excellence in teaching. 5. Demonstrated ability to teach a course on the American constitutional tradition and key texts of the Western political tradition that have influenced America’s political development. 6. Experience engaging with a variety of academic, administrative, and public audiences. Applications are welcome from disciplines related to the Institute’s mission. Such disciplines may include history, political science, philosophy, and legal studies. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will have expertise in at least one of the following areas: 1. American political thought, especially the American Founding. 2. American history 3. The development of American institutions 4. American constitutionalism Candidates with a secondary area of expertise in one of these areas are also welcome to apply. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) da36f84a Last Name (required) 20359651 Email (required) 748d00fd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Food Service Worker Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Food And Nutritional Svcs - 109760 Prepare and mixes ingredients for cold dishes and beverages. Make toast, prepares short order foods on grill and fried foods. Assembles food for patients and serves employees, visitors, and students. Delivers patient trays to bedside Server Administrator Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio IT Personnel - 105780 This position is responsible for the server administration and daily server operations of The University of Toledo’s server infrastructure including upgrades, installation, and troubleshooting of server related hardware, software, and applications. The Server Systems Administrator will provide Epic ECSA Web and Service Systems and/or ODB support related to install, troubleshooting, and assist with managing server systems. Creative Director Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio University Marketing - 104840 Impact on the Organization\n• Shapes the visual identity and brand experience of The University of Toledo and UToledo Health, influencing how prospective students, current students, patients, alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and community partners experience and perceive the institution.\n• Translates institutional and healthcare strategies into compelling creative that advances enrollment, student success, patient growth, philanthropic engagement, brand reputation, and other strategic priorities.\n• Ensures creative excellence, brand consistency, and an integrated visual identity across all marketing and communications channels, strengthening engagement with key audiences and supporting the long-term success of the University and UToledo Health. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a73f7d5b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Academic Employment Type Faculty - Regular Faculty - Regular Locations Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 13a6616d Last Name (required) d8001efa Email (required) dd56221c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
