    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/maintenance-repair-worker-2-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance Repair Worker 2",
      "description": "Maintenance Repair Worker 2 - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Maintenance Repair Worker 2 501514 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH CWA Full-Time Maintenance/Facilities Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Maintenance Repair Worker 2 Department Org: Maintenance/Structur - 105670 Employee Classification: H3 - Comm Workers of America FT Bargaining Unit: Communication Workers America Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 7:00am End Time: 3:30pm Posted Salary: $17.90 Float: False Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: False Job Description: Under general supervision, performs variety of semi-skilled and skilled maintenance duties for buildings and equipment including plumbing, electrical, painting, general maintenance, and carpentry. Assists skilled maintenance repair workers and skilled trades persons in maintenance repair work. Minimum Qualifications: • Must possess a High School diploma or equivalent GED. • 6 months training or 6 months experience in maintenance repair. • Valid driver’s license and insurability under UT driving policies. • Ability to read, understand and comprehend instructions such as work orders, assembly instructions, etc. • Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide whole numbers and to read and write simple sentences. Must have basic knowledge of mathematics to read a measuring tape and must be capable of working with fractions in order to work with measurements. • Skill in building and equipment maintenance and repair (e.g., electrical, plumbing, carpentry, painting, plastering, heating.) • Skill in use of associated hand and/or power tools and equipment (1 month experience or equivalent.) • Demonstrate dexterity and skillful use of hands. • Ability to lift, carry, and maneuver objects weighing up to 50 lbs., climb ladders or stairs, Able to stand for long periods, stoop, kneel and reach. • Ability to lift or move objects between 50-100 pounds with assistance. Communication and other skills: • Verbal skills to communicate with staff, family members, and management. • Verbal skills to communicate with other trades and work control. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Patient Registration Spec Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The Patient Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Basic Outpatient Presvc Spec Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The Basic Outpatient Preservice Specialist performs all outpatient scheduling, pre-registration and insurance verification for non-invasive, routine care services. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/account-clerk-3-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-f73f2982-515a-4ec2-8576-01e007f9a3bc": {
      "title": "Account Clerk 3",
      "description": "Account Clerk 3 - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Account Clerk 3 501524 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Administrative Support Full-Time Support Services Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Account Clerk 3 Department Org: Lab-Admin - 109380 Employee Classification: B1 - Classif'd Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 0800 End Time: 1630 Posted Salary: 18.41 - $ 20.75 Job Description: The Account Clerk 3 role provides revenue cycle and billing support for Clinical Pathology, Anatomic Pathology, Surgical Pathology, and Cytopathology. This position performs charge review, charge entry, coding support, account analysis, registration support, credit processing, and charge reconciliation in Epic and related systems. The role verifies appropriate Current Procedural terminology (CPT) and ICD-10-CM diagnosis coding information, monitors duplicate or missing charges, supports monthly revenue reporting, and serves as a liaison among the laboratory, Health Information Management (HIM), Patient Financial Services/Revenue Cycle, University of Toledo Medical Center clinics, provider offices, and the University of Toledo Physicians (UTP) practice plan. Work requires accuracy, attention to detail, timely follow-up, confidentiality, HIPAA compliance, and professional communication to support compliant reimbursement and high-quality patient care. Minimum Qualifications: • High school diploma required; associate degree in Accounting or Finance preferred. • Working knowledge of medical terminology, medical insurance, CPT coding, ICD-10-CM (diagnosis) coding, laboratory billing workflows, and health care reimbursement processes. • 1-3 years of recent work experience in medical billing, patient accounting, health information management, revenue cycle, or a related health care administrative function preferred. • General knowledge of reimbursement methodologies and payer requirements, including DRG, APC, per diem, capitation, fee-for-service, managed care, and governmental payers as applicable. • Understanding of HIPAA, patient confidentiality, corporate compliance, billing compliance, and applicable state and federal regulations. • Proficiency with Epic or comparable electronic health record/billing systems, Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, Outlook, and other software applications required for the position. • Ability to review accounts and data for accuracy, identify discrepancies, research issues, document follow-up, and resolve routine billing questions. • Strong oral and written communication skills, including professional communication with patients, providers, clinics, HIM, Revenue Cycle/Patient Financial Services, and laboratory staff. • Effective interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively with internal and external customers in a courteous and professional manner. • Ability to organize work, set priorities, meet deadlines, maintain attention to detail, and manage multiple follow-up items in a fast-paced environment. • Ability to work independently with minimal supervision while recognizing when escalation or leadership input is needed. • Ability to maintain strict confidentiality of patient, financial, operational, and sensitive department information. • Ability and willingness to adapt to changing regulatory, payer, system, and departmental requirements. • Demonstrates a strong work ethic, reliability, flexibility, and willingness to assist with overtime or additional assignments when required by department needs. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Patient Registration Spec Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The Patient Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Basic Outpatient Presvc Spec Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The Basic Outpatient Preservice Specialist performs all outpatient scheduling, pre-registration and insurance verification for non-invasive, routine care services. ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
