    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/seasonal-employee-hourly-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-113d56b2-adfd-4385-b862-1f78e4a5b098": {
      "title": "Seasonal Employee Hourly",
      "description": "Seasonal Employee Hourly - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Seasonal Employee Hourly 501590 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic Administration Administrative Support None Part-Time Support Services Show More Show Less Staff - Contingent Add to favorites View favorites Title: Seasonal Employee Hourly Department Org: Accessibility/Disability Resources - 104170 Employee Classification: H6 - Intermittent - Seasonal Hourly Bargaining Unit: Bargaining Unit Exempt Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Job Description: The Student Support Specialist will provide individualized academic access support to a blind student in classroom, laboratory, testing, tutoring, and other campus settings. The purpose of the role is to reduce disability-related access barriers while supporting the student’s independence and full participation. Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to exercise discretion and maintain the student’s confidentiality • Strong verbal communication skills, including the ability to clearly and objectively describe visual information • Experience working with blind or visually impaired individuals preferred • Experience providing tutoring or academic support preferred • Ability to maintain neutrality, confidentiality, and academic integrity while proctoring examinations • Dependable, responsible, punctual, and professional • Respectful of individual preferences, learning styles, and student autonomy • Ability to follow multi-step instructions and complete tasks efficiently • Comfortable using computers, learning-management systems, Microsoft Office applications, and other relevant technology • Ability to learn and safely operate classroom or laboratory equipment when necessary • Willingness to complete all required safety, confidentiality, and institutional training • Flexible availability based on the student’s class schedule, examinations, tutoring needs, and other academic responsibilities • Reliable transportation or ability to travel between assigned campus locations Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) a95bdce8 Last Name (required) 395b65ff Email (required) 03fe217d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Program Coordinator, IACTL Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio Inst Am Cons Thought & Ldrship - 114470 The Institute of Constitutional Thought & Leadership is looking to hire a Program Coordinator.  This role assists with planning and executing logistics for the Institute’s K-12 educational initiatives, as well as providing support for the Institute’s public-facing events. Lab Animal Aide - LAA Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio Dept of Lab Animal Resources - 100750 Full Time // Mon-Fri 7:15 AM - 3:45 PM // AFSCME C37\nProvides daily husbandry of laboratory animals to include observations of animals, handling and restraint, feeding and watering, changing cages/racks, and sanitizing animal areas and equipment. Maintains the facility in compliance with regulations and accrediting bodies. Provides a supportive role in the oversight of research activities to ensure compliance with approved protocols and regulations. Nurse Assistant Director - Inpatient Orthopedics, Med-Surg, & Float Pool Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Nursing Svcs Admin - 109920 Assistant Nursing Director (mostly between 2:00 pm - 10:30 pm) manages the day to day activities of patient care in orthopedic med-surg, nursing pool, and other ancillary departments under the direction of the unit nursing directors/managers/operations supervisors and acts in the absence of the unit nursing directors/managers/operations supervisors. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 46142c25 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Administration Administrative Support None Part-Time Support Services Academic Administration Administrative Support None Part-Time Support Services Employment Type Staff - Contingent Staff - Contingent Locations Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) bf1edc09 Last Name (required) 95692a0c Email (required) a7908158 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5