    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/staff-nurse-emergency-dept-ed-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-5ef80e8b-40e7-466f-80e9-51eaf443a9c5": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse",
      "description": "Staff Nurse - Emergency Dept. (ED) - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Staff Nurse - Emergency Dept. (ED) 501140 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Healthcare Positions Nursing Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Staff Nurse - Emergency Dept. (ED) Department Org: Emergency Dept. - 110080 Employee Classification: B5 - Unclass Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 3 Start Time: 7:00 pm End Time: 7:30 am Posted Salary: $ 33.63 - $ 43.64 Float: True Rotate: True On Call: True Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: Maintains standards of professional nursing practice and coordinates total nursing care for patients with consideration of their specific age needs. Provides leadership by working cooperatively with other health care professionals. Minimum Qualifications: Education / Knowledge / Skills / Abilities 1. Active RN licensure in the State of Ohio is required. 2. BLS required. 3. Must be willing to rotate shifts and units. 4. May be required to assume Charge Nurse role. 5. Physical requirements: a. visual acuity of 20/20 or corrected to 20/20 including color vision when applicable; b. ability to hear (with or without aides) c. ability to orally communicate d. good manual dexterity e. ability to push, pull, roll, and transfer/lift 50 pounds occasionally f. ability to stand, walk frequently g. ability to bend, reach, stoop, kneel frequently; and h. ability to perform CPR. Communication/Skills 1. Exhibits accuracy, integrity and flexibility; is punctual and dependable. 2. Possesses organizational, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills. 3. Demonstrates ability to work with self-direction and effectiveness under minimal supervision. 4. Demonstrates excellent written and verbal communication skills; possesses group facilitation skills. 5. Must have demonstrated ability in conflict negotiation and ability to exercise diplomacy and tact in potentially volatile situations. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 6f39c247 Last Name (required) efc1ef8d Email (required) e32ff76d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Program Coordinator, IACTL Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio Inst Am Cons Thought & Ldrship - 114470 The Institute of Constitutional Thought & Leadership is looking to hire a Program Coordinator.  This role assists with planning and executing logistics for the Institute’s K-12 educational initiatives, as well as providing support for the Institute’s public-facing events. Seasonal Employee Hourly Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio Accessibility/Disability Resources - 104170 The Student Support Specialist will provide individualized academic access support to a blind student in classroom, laboratory, testing, tutoring, and other campus settings. The purpose of the  role is to reduce disability-related access barriers while supporting the student’s independence and full participation. Lab Animal Aide - LAA Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio Dept of Lab Animal Resources - 100750 Full Time // Mon-Fri 7:15 AM - 3:45 PM // AFSCME C37\nProvides daily husbandry of laboratory animals to include observations of animals, handling and restraint, feeding and watering, changing cages/racks, and sanitizing animal areas and equipment. Maintains the facility in compliance with regulations and accrediting bodies. Provides a supportive role in the oversight of research activities to ensure compliance with approved protocols and regulations. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8fd868d5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories AFSCME Healthcare Positions Nursing AFSCME Healthcare Positions Nursing Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 014ad9ec Last Name (required) 36952ef2 Email (required) fe76f007 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you ↑ Facebook Instagram Tiktok X Youtube © 2026 THE UNIVERSITY OF TOLEDO • 2801 W. Bancroft St. • Toledo, OH 43606 • 800.586.5336 A - Z List | Careers | Report a Concern | Nondiscrimination | Accessibility | Web Privacy | Feedback | Contact Us | Cookie